American Revolution (1776) — The successful establishment of a sovereign republic, fundamentally shifting political power from monarchy to representative government in the colonies;

Haitian Revolution (1791–1804) — A globally significant success resulting in the establishment of the first free black republic and the complete abolition of slavery in the former French colony;

Velvet Revolution (1989) — A remarkably peaceful revolution in Czechoslovakia that successfully transitioned the nation from a Soviet-style communist regime to a democratic republic;

Cuban Revolution (1959) — Successfully overthrew the decades-long dictatorship of Fulgencio Batista, fundamentally restructuring Cuban society and establishing a new political system;

Indian Independence Movement (c. 1947) — While often a nationalist movement as much as a revolution, it successfully dismantled a massive imperial power structure and established the modern nation-state of India;

Tunisian Revolution (2011) — Led to the overthrow of the entrenched, autocratic Ben Ali regime, marking a successful transition toward democratic institutions in the Maghreb region.
